---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
const photo = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}assets/founder-photo.jpg`;
---
<PageLayout title="Behind the Lab" kicker="BEHIND THE LAB // building in public" lead="Homogmos Lab did not begin as an institution. It began as a question.">
<section><div class="photo-layout">
<div class="photo-placeholder" id="portrait-slot"><span>founder-photo.jpg</span><span>portrait placeholder // 4:5 recommended</span></div>
<div class="terminal prose"><p><span class="prompt">homogmos@station:~$</span> cat behind_the_lab.txt</p><h3 class="display">Building a laboratory, one question at a time.</h3>
<p>I am Guillermo Hernández, a computational biologist interested in evolutionary genomics, paleogenomics, population genetics and scientific software.</p>
<p>My work is driven by questions about processes we cannot observe directly: ancestry, divergence, local genealogies, extinct populations and the different histories preserved across genomes.</p>
<p>Rather than waiting for the perfect laboratory or the perfect opportunity, I decided to begin building one. Homogmos Lab is that experiment.</p>
<p>This laboratory is being built in public. Every project, article, tool, failed hypothesis and rewritten question becomes part of its history. The goal is not only to present finished science. It is to document scientific exploration.</p>
<div class="tags"><span>evolutionary genomics</span><span>bioinformatics</span><span>paleogenomics</span><span>population genetics</span><span>scientific computing</span><span>natural history</span></div>
</div></div></section>
<section><div class="split"><div class="prose"><h2>$ background</h2><p>My training spans experimental biology and integrative biology, with computational work in genomics, evolutionary analysis and data science. I work primarily with Python, R and Linux and have used tools and approaches for phylogenetics, coalescent analysis, molecular evolution, variant processing and reproducible scientific workflows.</p><p>This is intentionally not a résumé page. The strongest description of Homogmos Lab should be the work itself: research questions, public projects, software, methods and the record of how those projects evolve.</p></div><div class="prose"><h2>$ invitation</h2><p>If these ideas resonate with you, welcome. Whether you are a scientist, developer, student, artist or simply curious about evolution, I hope you find something here worth exploring.</p><p>Homogmos Lab is young. Some projects will become papers. Some will become software. Some may fail. Others may lead to questions we have not imagined yet.</p><p>That uncertainty is part of the laboratory.</p></div></div></section>
<script define:vars={{photo}} is:inline>
  const img = new Image(); img.src = photo;
  img.onload = () => { const slot=document.getElementById('portrait-slot'); if(slot){ slot.outerHTML=`<img class="profile-photo" src="${photo}" alt="Guillermo Hernández">`; } };
</script>
</PageLayout>